# Line endings are a correctness issue in this repository, not a style one.
#
# gradlew is a shell script executed on Linux and macOS. If Git hands a contributor a CRLF
# copy and it is committed back that way, the script stops working on every non-Windows
# machine - with an error that blames the shell rather than the line endings. A public samples
# repository is cloned on all three platforms by definition.
* text=auto eol=lf

# The Windows launcher is the one file that genuinely wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
*.cmd text eol=crlf

# Vendored AEP binaries and assets: never touched, never normalised, never diffed as text.
*.jar binary
*.aar binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png binary
